<h1>Find your official sample ballot</h1>
<p>Your sample ballot is the official list of contests and questions for your voting address. Use the county Board of Elections lookup to choose an election and ballot style.</p>

<p><a class="primary-action" href="https://lookup.boe.ohio.gov/vtrapp/ashtabula/ballotlist.aspx" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Open the Ashtabula County ballot lookup</a></p>

<h2>How to find the right ballot</h2>
<ol>
  <li>On the county lookup page, select the November 3, 2026 General Election.</li>
  <li>If you know your precinct, select the matching ballot style. If you do not, use the page’s voter-information search to identify your precinct first.</li>
  <li>Open the ballot and check that the precinct and districts match your voter registration.</li>
</ol>

<p>The candidate and issue pages in this guide help explain the choices. The county’s sample ballot confirms which contests and questions apply to your address. If the lookup is unclear or your ballot seems wrong, contact the <a href="https://www.boe.ohio.gov/ashtabula/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Ashtabula County Board of Elections</a>.</p>

